## What this deploys

One `google_cloud_run_v2_service` (`{{ deployments[0].serviceName }}` in
`{{ deployments[0].region }}`) running `{{ deployments[0].containerImage }}`
on port {{ deployments[0].port }}, with {{ deployments[0].cpuLimit }} CPU /
{{ deployments[0].memoryLimit }} memory per instance and scaling bounds
{{ deployments[0].minInstances }}..{{ deployments[0].maxInstances }} instances,
plus (only when `allow_unauthenticated = true`; currently
`{{ deployments[0].allowUnauthenticated }}`) an `allUsers` →
`roles/run.invoker` IAM member. Nothing else: no secrets, no domain
mappings, no service-account minting -- those are separate, deliberate
decisions, not side effects of a deploy module.

